=== task: mcq easy
title: A deque as a stack
prompt: Which pair of operations makes a deque work as a stack?
* `append` and `pop` :: Right. Both work at the right end: last in, first out.
- `append` and `popleft` :: In at one end and out at the other: that's a queue.
- `appendleft` and `pop` :: Also opposite ends: a queue going the other way.
- `rotate` and `pop` :: `rotate` moves items round; it doesn't add any.
