=== task: predict hard
title: Which end is dropped?
code:
```python
from collections import deque

d = deque([1, 2, 3], maxlen=3)
d.appendleft(0)
print(list(d))
d.append(4)
print(list(d))
d.rotate(1)
print(list(d))
```
wrong[[0, 1, 2, 3]\n[0, 1, 2, 3, 4]\n[4, 0, 1, 2, 3]]: `maxlen=3` means the deque never holds more than 3 items: each add to a full deque drops one from the other end.
wrong[[1, 2, 3]\n[2, 3, 4]\n[4, 2, 3]]: Adding at the left drops from the right: `appendleft(0)` drops the 3, not the 0.
